Midnight Battle Zone is a cat-themed 3D real-time strategy game written
in Rust, with a Vulkan renderer and Lua 5.4 scripting. Train Worker,
Soldier and Sniper Cats, mine crystals, build bases, and fight a Lua AI
at three difficulty levels on three battle maps, or play a two-player
LAN game with mDNS discovery.

It features fog of war, a minimap, AMD FidelityFX Super Resolution 1.0
upscaling, and public-domain jazz and blues background music. Units,
buildings and maps are defined in Lua and can be extended.

A Vulkan driver is required. Gamepads are supported through SDL3, and
sound plays through sndio's aucat (or PulseAudio's paplay).
